.PP
Token pasting refers to the \f[CR]##\f[R] operator in macros, used to
merge two tokens into one during preprocessing.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
#define AB(A, B) A##B

int AB(ma, in)(void) \f[I]// Expands to: int main(void)\f[R]
{
    . . .
}
.EE
